, the only matter is amount, Create Element can create eletricity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T00:02:53-07:00","id":1510959,"title":"","content":"Probably just disdain. Going so far as to kill him when he hasn't broken the litany or done anything wyrmy is a waste since he might still produce useful children. Maybe they'll treat him like ronin and extort him for all the fetishes and talens he's got. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, if he sets his bunker up on a node, IE an area like a caern, so that he can recover gnosis in his bunker, which he should if he really wants to use certain gifts like create element and last with any strength post-apoc, he's a target for extermination since a nobody shouldn't be hoarding that kind of thing and building a bunker there could be considered a violation of the sanctity of a caern. Of course, the werewolf could try to justify his bunker as &quot;me protecting this small sacred place, nevermind the concrete fortifications that may or may not disturb the natural flow of energy&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> Rat is pretty chill with his kids that just want to survive and not actively contribute to the war, but getting a lot of resources for this kinda thing is a no-no for bonegnawers. <br /> <br /> <br /> I had a character that, due to trauma, was obsessed with surviving anything and was prepping for the apocaylpse, but her strat didn't involve bunkers but in getting the abilities and gifts she needs to survive the worst conditions. As a lupus with short pregnancy times she also had a lot of kids in the hopes that they would bolster her survival chances, though she was a lousy parent. <br /> <br /> Resist toxin is great, but there's a lot of other low level gifts that greatly boost survival odds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}